			"Message": "fix(Shim/Cocoon): Improve type safety and error handling in IPC shims\n\n- Added explicit type annotations to error parameters in `ipcRendererShim`, `webFrameShim`, and configuration resolution logic to enhance type safety in the Cocoon extension host shim layer\n- Fixed static asset path construction in `Application.astro` by correcting `_VSCODE_FILE_ROOT` slash alignment, ensuring proper resource loading in Sky frontend\n- Removed redundant `slot=\"Head\"` attributes from worker scripts and added `defer` for optimized loading sequence\n- Updated development SSL certificates as part of routine security maintenance\n- Adjusted TypeScript configuration to enable experimental decorators and improved module resolution paths for VS Code source integration, supporting future shim development\n\nThese changes strengthen type safety in critical IPC communication paths between Mountain and Cocoon while ensuring proper environment detection (web vs desktop) in the Sky UI layer. The script loading optimizations contribute to Land's performance goals by ensuring non-blocking resource initialization.",
